PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round-2 consolidation: A bloc (2,3,4,6,8,10,11,12) now uniformly cites closed-form cumulative IRR
IR_v = [(1-p)(1-e^{-λT})] / [pT + (1-p)(1-e^{-λT})/λ] < (1-p)λ
for any finite T>0, directly implying IRR<1-p and 1-IRR>p (overestimate). B bloc (1,5,7,9,13,14) continues to invoke IRR(t)=(1-p)exp(pλt) trajectory but supplies no explicit integral or person-time weighting that overturns the closed-form result. The exact expressions already embed differential depletion via survival functions; they do not assume constant mixture proportions. No new counter-algebra appeared. Core distinction preserved: bias mechanism (protected PT inflation) is absent under leaky vaccines (constant HR=1-p) and vanishes only as T→0. My weight remains on A; B arguments conflate instantaneous hazard ratio with observable cumulative IRR.}

